            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="1064" n="970" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg970"/>

                <head>No. 601.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Baron Rosen to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Russian Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 19, 1887</date>.
                        (Received June 20.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am instructed to inform you that the
                    Imperial Government desires to propose to the governments who have expressed
                    that intention to take part in the labors of the Fourth International Prison
                    Congress in St. Petersburg to formulate, before the first day of September,
                    1887, the questions which they would like to submit for discussion at tike
                    congress, and also to communicate the names of the scientists who would be
                    willing to assume the task of reporting on any of the questions proposed for
                    discussion in the official programme of the congress drafted at the conference
                    of Berne.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rosen.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
